{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792496478,"nonce":"craD46XTiuIeyx3rAwuvhchm7ZY=","title":"Bound synchronous Markdown mounts and redundant SCM refresh work","message":"Profiling extension opening identifies native UI construction/layout as the main recurring input blocker. A 7,838-byte rich Markdown preview (eight Mermaid diagrams, 16 highlighted code fences and math) opens in 1.57 seconds AOT, including a 1.14-second UI turn; reactivation still takes 1.12 seconds without rerunning the Markdown renderer. A native stack sample captured all 731 main-thread samples below LayoutTree.computeLayout -\u003e hl_blinc_tree_compute_layout while both extension workers were parked.\n\nVirtualize Markdown blocks, retaining parsed data and lightweight layout measurements while mounting only visible content. Keep the existing inactive-view cleanup and image residency behavior. Bound the work passed to native layout before trying to optimize the VM.\n\nThe Git sidebar additionally calls refresh() for every active.changed event. It rereads status, walks history and replaces reactive lists and selected-commit deltas even when repository data is unchanged; avoid unchanged assignments and unnecessary history reloads while preserving explicit refresh, file-save and external-change handling.\n\nReproduce with scripts/extension-bench.sh and scripts/extension-bench.sh --native. RAYDE_PROBE_MARKDOWN selects a source; raw timing/model/node counts and worker logs are in bin/extension-bench. Native evidence is in bin/extension-stress-stack/sample.txt. See the profiling issue for the full table and environment.","files":null}]}